# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you have. Everything is optional —
# sources without configuration show an honest "not configured" empty state.
# There is no mock data: every number you see comes from a real source.
#
# Desktop app: the same keys can be placed in `opsora.env` inside the OS
# app-data directory (a commented template is written on first launch).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- GitHub
# Fine-grained or classic PAT. Read-only access to repos, issues, actions.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Pi-hole
# Base URL of the Pi-hole (v6 API) and its password.
PIHOLE_URL=http://pi.hole
PIHOLE_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Docker
# Docker is detected automatically at /var/run/docker.sock.
# Set OPSORA_DOCKER=0 to opt out, or override the socket path.
# OPSORA_DOCKER=
# DOCKER_SOCKET=/var/run/docker.sock
#
# Docker Compose only: when the socket is mounted into the container, set
# DOCKER_GID to the host docker group GID so the non-root container user can
# read it. Find yours with: stat -c '%g' /var/run/docker.sock
# DOCKER_GID=983

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Agent
# Shared secret required from /api/agent when set.
# OPSORA_AGENT_TOKEN=
# Where ingested metrics are persisted between restarts.
# OPSORA_DATA_DIR=.data

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Alerts
# Server-side alert delivery. The dispatcher checks the attention feed every
# minute and pushes new critical/warning signals to configured channels.
# Disable entirely with OPSORA_ALERTS=0. OPSORA_ALERT_LEVEL=all includes info.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
# OPSORA_ALERT_INTERVAL=60000
# OPSORA_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:9942

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Google Calendar
# Create an OAuth client (Desktop app) in Google Cloud, then run:
#   node scripts/google-oauth.mjs
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# Defaults to "primary". A calendar id or email also works.
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID=
